  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Find the disjoint union of the sets ${3,6,9}$ and ${p,q,r}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that the sets are disjoint since\n\n$$\n{3,6,9}\\cap {p,q,r}=\u2205.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the disjoint union is simply the union:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3,6,9}\u2294{p,q,r} & ={3,6,9}\\cup {p,q,r} \\\\  & ={3,6,9,p,q,r}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
